                <section>
                    <div class='title'>
                        <h1 id='ALAS2023-2026-3302'>ALAS2023-2026-3302</h1>
                    </div>

                    <div class='text'>
                        <hr class='mid-pad'>
                        <span class='alas-info'>
                            <b>Amazon Linux 2023 Security Advisory:</b> ALAS2023-2026-3302
                        </span><br />
                        <span class='alas-info'><b>Advisory Released Date:</b> 2026-10-22 </span><br />
                        <span class='alas-info'><b>Advisory Updated Date:</b> 2026-10-22 </span><br />

                        <div id='severity' class='alas-info'>
                            <b>Severity:</b>
                            <span class='date'>
                                <span class='bulletin-type'>
                                    <i class='fas fa-exclamation-triangle'></i>
                                </span>
                            </span>
                            Important<br />
                        </div>

                        <div id='references'>
                            <b>References:</b>
                            
                                <a href='https://explore.alas.aws.amazon.com/CVE-2026-109618.html' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>CVE-2026-109618&nbsp;</a>
                                                            
                            
                                <a href='https://explore.alas.aws.amazon.com/CVE-2026-109619.html' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>CVE-2026-109619&nbsp;</a>
                                                            
                            <br />
                            <a href="../../faqs.html">FAQs regarding Amazon Linux ALAS/CVE Severity</a>
                        </div>

                        <hr class='mid-pad'>
                        <div id='issue_overview'>
                            <b>Issue Overview:</b><br>
                            
                                <p>PHP uses longjmp() for out-of-memory (OOM) errors to exit the current context and abort handling of the request. Some contexts may not properly account for this scenario and leave request memory in an uninitialized state before performing an allocation. The subsequent request cleanup procedure may read or branch on this memory. Multiple OOM strategies can consistently trigger this condition and lead to remote code execution (RCE). (CVE-2026-109618)</p><p>PHP has various global state that temporarily points into request memory. In some scenarios, global state may not be correctly reset, or may be repopulated after being reset. The global state may then refer to request memory even after it has been freed. Subsequent requests may read or branch on this stale state before it is fully initialized. Multiple strategies can trigger this condition and produce remote code execution (RCE). (CVE-2026-109619)</p>
                            
                        </div>

                        <div id='affected_packages' class='alas-info'>
                            <br />
                            <b>Affected Packages:</b>
                            <br />
                            <p>php8.3</p>
                        </div>

                        <div id="issue_correction">
<br/>
<b>Issue Correction:</b>
<br/>
Run <i>dnf update php8.3 --releasever 2023.12.20261021</i> or <i>dnf update --advisory ALAS2023-2026-3302 --releasever 2023.12.20261021</i> to update your system.<br/>More information on how to update your system can be found on this page: <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/linux/al2023/ug/managing-repos-os-updates.html">Amazon Linux 2023 documentation</a><br /></div>
                        <br />
                        <div id='new_packages'>
                            <b>New Packages:</b><pre>aarch64:<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-cli-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-common-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-mbstring-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-ffi-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-fpm-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-gd-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-bcmath-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-snmp-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-pspell-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-fpm-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-modphp-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-dbg-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-opcache-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-intl-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-opcache-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-dbg-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-soap-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-modphp-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-debugsource-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-mbstring-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-xml-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-xml-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-mysqlnd-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-process-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-mysqlnd-8.3.36-1.amzn2023.0.1.aarch64<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; php8.3-pgsql-debuginfo-8.3.36-1.a